  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_Site_v1__area">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_Site_v1"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_Area_v1"/>
    <rdfs:label>contains Area</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Reference to a contained area of the site</rdfs:comment>
    <isa95:sourceComment>Not part of the ISA-95 Standard. Just to make the graph easier to handle</isa95:sourceComment>
    <isa95:sourceDtmi>dtmi:digitaltwins:isa95:Site;1#area</isa95:sourceDtmi>
    <isa95:dtdlType>Relationship</isa95:dtdlType>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_WorkCenter_v1__workUnit">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_WorkCenter_v1"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_WorkUnit_v1"/>
    <rdfs:label>contains Work unit</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Reference to a contained work unit of the work center</rdfs:comment>
    <isa95:sourceComment>Not part of the ISA-95 Standard. Just to make the graph easier to handle</isa95:sourceComment>
    <isa95:sourceDtmi>dtmi:digitaltwins:isa95:WorkCenter;1#workUnit</isa95:sourceDtmi>
    <isa95:dtdlType>Relationship</isa95:dtdlType>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_LangStringSet_v1__langString">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_LangStringSet_v1"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:label>langString</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A set of strings, each annotated by the language of the string. The meaning of the stringin each language shall be the same.</rdfs:comment>
    <isa95:sourceDtmi>dtmi:digitaltwins:isa95:LangStringSet;1#langString</isa95:sourceDtmi>
    <isa95:dtdlType>Property</isa95:dtdlType>
    <isa95:writable>True</isa95:writable>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_ext_Tags_v1__markers">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_ext_Tags_v1"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:label>markers</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A marker tag is a simple string that is used to mark or categorize a digital twin, such as 'blue' or 'red'. This string is the tag's name, and marker tags have no meaningful value—the tag is significant just by its presence (or absence).</rdfs:comment>
    <isa95:sourceDtmi>dtmi:digitaltwins:isa95:ext:Tags;1#markers</isa95:sourceDtmi>
    <isa95:dtdlType>Property</isa95:dtdlType>
    <isa95:writable>True</isa95:writable>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
  <owl:DatatypeProperty rdf:about="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_ext_Tags_v1__values">
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/trumpf/isa95/digitaltwins_isa95_ext_Tags_v1"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:label>values</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>A value tag is a key-value pair that is used to give each tag a value, such as 'color': 'blue' or 'color': 'red'. Once a value tag is created, it can also be used as a marker tag by ignoring the tag's value.</rdfs:comment>
    <isa95:sourceDtmi>dtmi:digitaltwins:isa95:ext:Tags;1#values</isa95:sourceDtmi>
    <isa95:dtdlType>Property</isa95:dtdlType>
    <isa95:writable>True</isa95:writable>
  </owl:DatatypeProperty>
</rdf:RDF>
